# The inference ENGINE images a bundle should carry.
#
# Everything else in the bundle is read out of a helmfile render. The engine is
# not: a model service comes in from a `MODELS=` file on the command line (see
# models/examples/sglang-qwen.yaml), and a bundle is built before anyone knows
# which models the site will run -- so no render names it and no rule can infer
# it. Name it here instead.
#
# The four sidecars around it -- hang-watcher, CART and CART's two -- need no
# entry: the bundle reads those out of the engine chart's own values.yaml --
# hang-watcher and CART at the versions that chart pins, CART's ha and reload at
# versions.autoconfig from the environment, since those two are autoconfig's --
# and `registryMode` places them under `registry` like every other image of ours.
#
# Copy to offline/engine-images.txt and edit. An address here does two things:
# the bundle carries the image, and its host joins mirror-hosts.txt, so under
# `registryMode: mirror` an air-gapped node redirects it instead of reaching
# that host for real.
#
# NOT taken from the charts' defaults on purpose. They are
# `lmsysorg/sglang:latest` and `vllm/vllm-openai:latest-cu129-ubuntu2404`:
# floating tags that match nothing any cluster here runs.
#
# ⚠️ Size. One engine image is around 19 GB compressed -- bigger than the rest
#    of the bundle put together (17 GB for 68 images). Name only the engines
#    that site will actually run.
#
# Model weights are not here either, and are not a job for this bundle.

# The official images, pinned -- what models/examples/sglang-qwen.yaml asks for:
# lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.15-cu129
# vllm/vllm-openai:v0.21.0-cu129

# A site that builds its own engine images names them here instead, with the
# same tags the model entry asks for:
# <your-registry>/sglang:v0.5.15-cu129
# <your-registry>/vllm/vllm-openai:v0.21.0-cu129
